  "text": "One account shows Fráech swimming without clothes toward his love. A sea storei rose up and tried to take from him the joy of the meeting. He could not give the price that Medb and Ailill asked, for they wanted his magical cattle of the Otherworld. The girl was carried to a stronghold in the Alps, and the hero freed her. During the raid on the province of Ulster, Medb gave the girl to any warrior who would fight the hero. Fráech answered the call. He lost the duel and died. The girl then died of grief.",
